Alex Oren, cunningly disguised as response@myrealbox.com wrote:

> There are several DLLs that can be used with the altkeyhandler option,
> yet there is no documentation or explanation about them.
>
> What are the differences between nh340key, nhraykey and nhdefkey DLLs
> when running on Win2K?

Normally, you won't have to use any of these, for example when you're
using a standard IBM keyboard layout, with the US or UK keyboard handler.

If, for example, you're using the US international keyboard handler, you
might experience problems using the ^ or " keys. In this case, just try
each of the keyboard handlers, until you've found one that works for you.
If the problem occurs with each of them, you're out of luck, and you may
experiment with "subkeyvalue" option, which appears later in the sample
defaults.nh file.

